3060. User Activities within Time Bounds
Table: Sessions
Column Name	Type
user_id	int
session_start	datetime
session_end	datetime
session_id	int
session_type	enum

session_id is unique for each row.

session_type is an ENUM with two possible values: 'Viewer' and 'Streamer'.
This table records user sessions with start/end times and type.

Problem

Write a SQL query to find all users who have had at least two sessions of the same type (either Viewer or Streamer) with a maximum gap of 12 hours between those sessions.
Return the result ordered by user_id in ascending order.

Example
Input — Sessions table:
user_id	session_start	session_end	session_id	session_type
101	2023-11-01 08:00:00	2023-11-01 09:00:00	1	Viewer
101	2023-11-01 10:00:00	2023-11-01 11:00:00	2	Streamer
102	2023-11-01 13:00:00	2023-11-01 14:00:00	3	Viewer
102	2023-11-01 15:00:00	2023-11-01 16:00:00	4	Viewer
101	2023-11-02 09:00:00	2023-11-02 10:00:00	5	Viewer
102	2023-11-02 12:00:00	2023-11-02 13:00:00	6	Streamer
101	2023-11-02 13:00:00	2023-11-02 14:00:00	7	Streamer
102	2023-11-02 16:00:00	2023-11-02 17:00:00	8	Viewer
103	2023-11-01 08:00:00	2023-11-01 09:00:00	9	Viewer
103	2023-11-02 20:00:00	2023-11-02 23:00:00	10	Viewer
103	2023-11-03 09:00:00	2023-11-03 10:00:00	11	Viewer
Output:
user_id
102
103

Solution 1
===========
WITH x AS (
    SELECT
        user_id,
        session_type,
        session_start,
        LAG(session_end) OVER (
            PARTITION BY user_id, session_type
            ORDER BY session_start
        ) AS prev_end
    FROM Sessions
)
SELECT DISTINCT user_id
FROM x
WHERE prev_end IS NOT NULL
  AND TIMESTAMPDIFF(HOUR, prev_end, session_start) BETWEEN 0 AND 12
ORDER BY user_id;

Solution 2
===========
SELECT DISTINCT s1.user_id
FROM Sessions s1
JOIN Sessions s2
  ON s1.user_id = s2.user_id
 AND s1.session_type = s2.session_type
 AND s2.session_start > s1.session_start
 AND s2.session_start <= DATE_ADD(s1.session_start, INTERVAL 12 HOUR)
ORDER BY s1.user_id;
